/**
\page search_lane iccApplySearch: constrained Search-CMM lane

\tableofcontents

\section search_contract Input forms and sequence constraint

`iccApplySearch` applies a Search CMM to color data.

| Form | Token shape |
|---|---|
| JSON | `iccApplySearch -cfg config_file` |
| Direct | `iccApplySearch [-exportcfg file|-exportcfganddata file] [-debugcalc] data encoding interpolation search-sequence` |

The JSON lane requires exactly `-cfg file`; surplus tokens fail rather than
silently disappear. The direct lane removes `argv[0]`, consumes optional
export and debugging prefixes, then uses `CIccCfgDataApply::fromArgs()` followed
by `CIccCfgSearchApply::fromArgs()`. After either lane, the sequence must
contain exactly two or three profiles.

\dotfile search-lane.dot "iccApplySearch configuration, sequence, and output lane"

\section search_options Controls and data formats

| Control | Values or form | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| Export | `-exportcfg file`, `-exportcfganddata file` | Emit a JSON configuration, optionally including color data. |
| Debug | `-debugcalc` | Preserve calculator trace records in the output data. |
| Final encoding | 0 through 6 with optional precision and digits | Value, percent, unit float, float, 8-bit, 16-bit, or V2 16-bit plus formatting. |
| Interpolation | 0 or 1 | Linear or tetrahedral. |
| Search profiles | profile/intents with optional `-ENV:` controls | Defines the two- or three-profile search sequence. |

Configuration input can supply inline JSON color data, an external JSON color
data file, IT8 data, or legacy data. Direct mode requires legacy input data.
Output can be legacy, JSON color data, or IT8.

\section search_pcs PCS source encoding branch

Once `CIccConnectCmm::CreateSearch()` establishes the source space, a PCS
input is remapped to the corresponding device signature for conversion. The
wide PCS encodings float, unit-float, and percent disable clipping before
`ToInternalEncoding()`.

\section search_qa QA example

`iccApplySearch-quick-check.sh` covers each final encoding, both interpolation
modes, base intents, JSON export/replay, and invalid argument rejection.
*/
